# GRC Gravel App — Cursor AI Rules
# Victor Dawa · Gravel Riders Club Kenya · gravelriders.club

## Project
Full-stack PWA for Gravel Riders Club Kenya. Members join rides, register for races,
book bike repairs, track achievements, and connect via a social feed.

## Stack
- Next.js 14 App Router + TypeScript
- Supabase (auth, database, realtime)
- Tailwind CSS (dark theme)
- M-Pesa Daraja (STK Push payments)
- Vercel deployment

## Design System
- Background: #0D0F14 (pages), #1A1E2A (cards), #252B3B (inputs/accents)
- Primary accent: #F5C518 (GRC yellow)
- Text: #F0F2F5 (primary), #8892A4 (muted)
- Borders: #1E2436
- Danger: #EF4444 | Success: #22C55E | Info: #60A5FA
- Headings: 'Barlow Condensed' font (fontFamily: "'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif")
- Body: 'Space Grotesk' font
- Mobile-first: max-width 430px centered

## Architecture Rules
- Use SERVER components by default (no 'use client' unless needed for interactivity/hooks)
- Supabase: import from @/lib/supabase/server for server components, @/lib/supabase/client for client
- All data fetching in page.tsx (server), pass as props to *Client.tsx (client)
- Server actions live in actions.ts files, API routes in /app/api/
- Types in @/lib/types/database.ts — always import from there
- Utilities in @/lib/utils.ts (formatKES, formatRideDate, getInitials, etc.)

## Patterns
- Cards: background #1A1E2A, borderRadius 16px, border '1px solid #1E2436'
- Buttons: use .btn-primary (yellow) or .btn-secondary (dark) CSS classes from globals.css
- Inputs: use .grc-input CSS class from globals.css
- All amounts are KES — use formatKES() from @/lib/utils
- Dates: use formatRideDate(), formatFullDate(), formatTime() from @/lib/utils
- Member initials: use getInitials() from @/lib/utils
- Tier colors: use getTierColor() from @/lib/utils

## Database Tables (Supabase)
- profiles — member data, stats, tier, role
- rides — club ride events
- ride_registrations — who's registered for which ride
- race_events — Full Gas Criterium series
- race_registrations — race entries with M-Pesa payment
- repair_bookings — Wrench doorstep repair bookings
- mechanics — mechanic profiles
- posts — social feed posts
- post_likes — feed engagement
- member_badges — earned achievements
- badge_definitions — badge catalog
- mpesa_transactions — payment audit trail
- notifications — user notifications

## M-Pesa
- STK Push via /api/mpesa/stkpush — POST {phone, amount, accountReference, transactionDesc, referenceType, referenceId}
- Callback at /api/mpesa/callback — Safaricom posts here on payment result
- Status polling at /api/mpesa/status?checkoutRequestId=xxx
- Phone normalization: 07XXXXXXXX → 2547XXXXXXXX (use normalizePhone() from utils)
- All amounts in KES integers

## Admin
- Only users with role 'admin' or 'super_admin' can access /admin
- Victor Dawa is super_admin — set this in Supabase after first signup
- Admin layout handles role check and redirects unauthorized users

## Naming Conventions
- Page data-fetching: page.tsx (server component)
- Client interactivity: *Client.tsx (with 'use client')
- Server actions: actions.ts (with 'use server')
- API routes: route.ts
- Reusable components: PascalCase in /components/[module]/

## Never Do
- Never use localStorage (use Supabase for persistence)
- Never hardcode Supabase URLs or keys in components (use env vars)
- Never skip TypeScript types — import from @/lib/types/database.ts
- Never use Inter, Arial, or system fonts — always Barlow Condensed or Space Grotesk
- Never use white/light backgrounds — this is a dark theme app
- Never expose SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY to the client

## Commands
- Dev: npm run dev (http://localhost:3000)
- Type check: npx tsc --noEmit
- Build: npm run build
- Deploy: vercel --prod
